$DIR/test.p:4:11: x (variable of type int) is not constant
    A constant's value must be known when compiling: a literal, another
    constant, or an expression of those. A variable or function call is only
    known at run time. Declare a variable instead.
    (see "Constant declarations" in the Plutonium spec, section 10.6)
    (run "pluto explain E0013" for a longer explanation)
